{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>Upon the breastpiece.</b> For the breastpiece — to fasten them in its rings, as is explained below in the matter." "<b>Cords of.</b> A term of the roots of a tree, which hold onto the tree to grasp and to take hold in the ground — so too these will hold onto the breastpiece; by them it will be suspended on the ephod. And they are the two chains mentioned above in the matter of the settings. And Menachem ben Saruk also interpreted שַׁרְשְׁרוֹת as a term of roots, and said that the resh is superfluous, like the mem in שִׁלְשׁוֹם and the mem in רֵיקָם. But I do not accept his view; rather, שַׁרְשֶׁרֶת in the Hebrew tongue is like שַׁלְשֶׁלֶת in the language of the Mishnah." "<b>At the edge.</b> This is the edge mentioned above — you shall fasten them in the rings that will be at the edge of the breastpiece. And every גְּבוּל is a term for edge; אשומי״יל בְּלַעַז." "<b>The work of a plait.</b> Braided work."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {2 "the la'az is Old French asembler, 'to assemble/join' — the edge or border where things meet"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:55:16.928150454Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}